    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimization for LawDog highlights **Cal Raleigh** as our premier start with a score of 71.46. He benefits from a favorable matchup against Ray, where the SP\u2019s 4.95 xERA and **Cal Raleigh**\u2019s positive platoon edge create an ideal environment for power production. Right behind him, **Dylan Beavers** (64.87), **Masyn Winn** (63.85), and **Jonathan Aranda** (63.20) anchor the lineup. **Masyn Winn** is a critical asset today; while his base projection is modest, the favorable SP matchup and his 85% success rate in stolen base opportunities\u2014our scarcest category\u2014provide the efficiency boost necessary to solidify his spot. **JJ Bleday** also demands attention, as his score is inflated by a significant park factor, allowing him to overcome a negative platoon split against Feltner.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Tyler Freeman**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 46.75. While his park factor is excellent, he is stifled by the matchup against Greene, who possesses an elite 2.51 xERA, and a lower-order lineup assignment that suppresses his counting stat potential. We have also opted to keep **Jung Hoo Lee** in reserve (45.23) given the tough matchup against Logan Gilbert. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remaining on the IL and **Lawrence Butler** out of today\u2019s lineup, our depth is being tested, but the current configuration maximizes our daily efficiency score. We will monitor the weather closely, though all starters currently clear the \"Below floor\" threshold, ensuring we preserve our game caps while aggressively pursuing gains in AVG and SB.",
